"epo"><addressbook><name>MORITA HISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIBUTANI RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKETANI NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIBE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORITA, HISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBUTANI, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKETANI, NOBUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A color demodulating device having a reduced device scale by commonly using part of a processing circuit and having a performance on color demodulation equivalent to that of the prior art. An adding circuit (10) and a SW circuit (11) shifts the phase of the ramp waveform generated by a VCO circuit (9) alternately to 90 degrees and 180 degrees for every clock. A SIN data generating circuit (12) generates a phase alternating SIN wave signal from the phase-shifted ramp waveform. A multiplying circuit (3) carries out multiplexing for R-Y and B-Y demodulations on the basis of the phase alternating SIN wave signal. A cumulative adding circuit (6) adds burst signals cumulatively for the demodulated multiplexed R-Y signal and the B-Y signal. A second load holding circuit (8) outputs the R-Y burst signal and the B-Y burst signal separately and respectively to the VCO circuit (9) and a comparing circuit (13) to form feedback loops. A first load holding circuit (5) separates the R-Y signal and the B-Y signal from the multiplexed signal and outputs them.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif de démodulation couleur qui possède des dimensions réduites grâce à l'utilisation courante d'une partie d'un circuit de traitement et qui manifeste des performances de démodulation couleur équivalentes à celles des dispositifs des techniques précédentes. Un circuit additionneur (10) et un circuit d'ondes courtes OC (11) décalent la phase de la forme d'onde en rampe générée par un circuit d'oscillateur accordé par tension OAT (9) en alternance à 90 DEG  et à 180 DEG  pour chaque horloge. Un circuit de génération de données SIN (12) génère un signal d'onde SIN alternant en phase à partir de la forme d'onde en rampe décalée en phase. Un circuit multiplicateur (3) effectue le multiplexage pour les modulations R-Y et B-Y sur la base du signal d'onde SIN alternant en phase. Un circuit additionneur cumulatif (6) additionne cumulativement les signaux en rafale pour le signal R-Y multiplexé démodulé et le signal B-Y. Un deuxième circuit de maintien de charge (8) émet le signal en rafale R-Y et le signal en rafale B-Y séparément et à destination du circuit OAT (9) et d'un circuit comparateur (13), respectivement, pour former des boucles à rétroaction. Un premier circuit de maintien de charge (5) sépare les signaux R-Y et B-Y du signal multiplexé et les émet.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>